---
/*
 * The site footer — wordmark, section links, social column, legal row.
 *
 * It lived inline in `index.astro` until the legal pages shipped without any
 * footer at all: a reader who reached /privacy from a search result had no way
 * back into the site and no sight of the other legal documents. Extracting it
 * is what makes "every page ends the same way" true by construction rather
 * than by nine copies staying in sync.
 *
 * The section links are absolute (`/#work`, not `#work`) so they work from a
 * legal page as well as from the landing page, where the browser treats them
 * as a same-document fragment navigation and just scrolls. GlassNav's links
 * are absolute for the same reason.
 *
 * The slim one-line footer on six pages is left alone, for two different
 * reasons that were originally stated as one. /security, /spec and /download
 * carry a per-page right-hand tag ("acknowledgment-only · no bounty yet",
 * "spec status · draft · v0.1", "checksums signed · open") that this footer
 * has no slot for. /releases, /roadmap and /themes carry StatusBadge +
 * VersionBadge, byte-identical to the pair below — nothing stops them adopting
 * this footer, they are simply not migrated yet.
 *
 * NO IMPRESSUM LINK HERE, and it is not an oversight. impressum.astro's own
 * banner ("NOT LINKED, NOT INDEXED, ON PURPOSE") and astro.config.mjs's
 * sitemap filter both say the address is still a placeholder, and that an
 * incomplete Impressum is a WORSE position than a missing one because it is
 * the classic Abmahnung target precisely for looking compliant. The footer
 * link, the sitemap filter and the page's `robots` prop were designed to drop
 * together when the ladungsfähige Anschrift lands (example-org/operations#9).
 * Advertising the page from ten pages while its address is missing does not
 * satisfy § 5 DDG — reachability is not the element that is missing — it only
 * enlarges the surface of the gap.
 *
 * THE OTHER THREE LEGAL LINKS ARE GONE TOO, as of 2026-10-16, and they use the
 * same mechanism for the same reason: kept, reachable by URL, not advertised.
 * /terms/ and /nutzungsbedingungen/ are the hosted-sync beta terms, and the
 * offering they are the terms of is closed; /law-enforcement/,
 * /behoerdenanfragen/, /notice/ and /meldung/ describe what a server Myne
 * operates holds and how to notify it about content, and Myne operates no such
 * server (the 0696 decision entry in the main repo). The privacy policy DOES
 * stay linked: it is still a live document (the app stores require one), it
 * still covers the app and the download origin, and it is the page a reader is
 * likeliest to want. All six unlinked pages still build and still carry their
 * own notices;
 * they are `robots="noindex,nofollow"` and excluded in the astro.config sitemap
 * filter. This is deliberately reversible in three edits, because the legal
 * read that would confirm it has not happened yet.
 *
 * Coverage, stated honestly because "six pages still lack it" understates it:
 * 133 of 143 built pages have no legal row at all, including the whole
 * /user-guide/ subtree and /ledger/. Two shared layouts would cover most of
 * that in one edit (UserGuideShellLayout, LedgerFeedLayout).
 */
import StatusBadge from "./StatusBadge.astro";
import VersionBadge from "./VersionBadge.astro";
---

<footer style="padding:60px 28px 30px;">
  <div style="max-width:1280px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div
      class="mono up foot-nav"
      style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,1fr);gap:20px;font-size:11px;color:#8a8a86;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);padding:22px 0;"
    >
      <a href="/#work" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">How it works</a>
      <a href="/#capab" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Compare</a>
      <a href="/#commit" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">FAQ</a>
      <a href="/ledger/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Ledger</a>
      <a
        href="/user-guide/getting-started/welcome/"
        style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Guide</a
      >
      <a href="/themes/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Themes</a>
      <a href="/roadmap/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Roadmap</a>
    </div>
    <div
      style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;margin-top:30px;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;"
    >
      {/* A logo, not a section. `aria-hidden` keeps it out of the heading
          outline: on the landing page a decorative final heading was a
          flourish, but nine legal documents now end with it, and those are
          exactly the documents people navigate structurally. The visual result
          is unchanged. */}
      <h2
        aria-hidden="true"
        style="font-size:clamp(72px,18vw,260px);line-height:0.8;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.03em;"
      >
        Myne
      </h2>
      <div
        class="mono up"
        style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;font-size:11px;color:#54544f;text-align:right;"
      >
        <a
          href="https://github.com/myne-md"
          style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">GitHub</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://social.myne.md/@myne"
          rel="me"
          style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Mastodon</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://x.com/myne_md"
          rel="me noopener"
          style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">X</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://bsky.app/profile/myne.md"
          rel="me noopener"
          style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Bluesky</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.reddit.com/r/myne_md/"
          rel="me noopener"
          style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">Reddit</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- The clearance below is NOT decorative spacing — it is the wordmark's
         descender, and a flat `margin-top:26px` put this row underneath it.

         The "Myne" h2 above is `font-size:clamp(72px,18vw,260px)` with
         `line-height:0.8`, i.e. a line box deliberately SHORTER than the
         glyphs. Measured in the browser at 1600px: font-size 260px, box
         208px, natural line box 299px — so the half-leading is negative and
         the tail of the "y" paints 45.5px BELOW the h2's border box, while
         this row started only 26px below it. Net 19.5px of overlap, and the
         descender landed on top of "Terms".

         It was always this way; the legal links only made it visible,
         because the copyright text alone did not sit under the "y".

         The fix goes here rather than on the h2 on purpose. Giving the h2
         padding (or a line-height that contains its own ink) would work,
         but the flex row is `align-items:flex-end` and the social column
         is flush with the h2's box bottom — measured difference exactly
         0px — so growing that box drags the social links down with it and
         breaks an alignment nobody asked us to change.

         The overhang is 0.175 × font-size (45.5/260, measured), and
         font-size is itself a clamp, so the clearance has to be one too:
         0.175 × clamp(72px,18vw,260px) = clamp(12.6px,3.15vw,45.5px), plus
         the 26px this row was always meant to have. Change one of these two
         clamps and the other needs recomputing. -->
    <div
      class="mono up"
      style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:clamp(40px,calc(3.15vw + 26px),72px);font-size:10px;color:#54544f;"
    >
      <span
        >© 2026 · AGPL-3.0 · CC-BY-4.0 docs · <a
          href="/privacy/"
          style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"
          >Privacy</a
        ></span
      ><StatusBadge /><VersionBadge />
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style is:global>
  /* Footer link grid: seven across is too tight on a phone. */
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .foot-nav {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr) !important;
      gap: 14px 16px !important;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 460px) {
    .foot-nav {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr) !important;
    }
  }
</style>
